From: Camera investigation <camera-investigation@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH candidate] media: qcom: camss: Select MIPI RAW mode for VFE 680 RDI

The RDI path writes a MIPI RAW stream. Select the write master RAW
dump mode rather than leaving the mode field at its reset value.
VFE 480 already selects MIPI RAW for its RDI write masters.

An independent X1E80100 experiment reports image violations with mode
zero. Test frame layout, buffer bounds and all supported RDI formats on
full and lite VFEs before integrating this candidate.

Link: https://github.com/karsies-wq/sp11-imx681-linux/tree/b08f76f40b8d7b715bd4da6aef484f86142cc147

---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-680.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-vfe-680.c
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 
 #define VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG(vfe, c)	((vfe_is_lite(vfe) ? 0x400 : 0xe00) + (c) * 0x100)
 #define		VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG_EN	BIT(0)
+#define		VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG_MIPI_RAW	BIT(16)
 #define VFE_BUS_IMAGE_ADDR(vfe, c)		((vfe_is_lite(vfe) ? 0x404 : 0xe04) + (c) * 0x100)
 #define VFE_BUS_FRAME_INCR(vfe, c)		((vfe_is_lite(vfe) ? 0x408 : 0xe08) + (c) * 0x100)
 #define VFE_BUS_IMAGE_CFG0(vfe, c)		((vfe_is_lite(vfe) ? 0x40c : 0xe0c) + (c) * 0x100)
@@ -186,7 +187,7 @@
 	vfe_disable_irq(vfe);
 
 	/* Enable WM */
-	writel(VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG_EN,
+	writel(VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG_EN | VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG_MIPI_RAW,
 	       vfe->base + VFE_BUS_WRITE_CLIENT_CFG(vfe, wm));
 
 	dev_dbg(vfe->camss->dev, "RDI%d WM:%d width %d height %d stride %d\n",
